Z||000004||Chris McDonald||02-02-2001||10:25 AM||||<BR>When I look at them it says they have a 4 cylinder but 0-60 times are 5 seconds?  Want kind of steroids is it on or do the people that make them measure their engines to different standards?[/B][/QUOTE]<P>I take care of a 1990 Lotus Esprit Turbo for a good friend of mine.  His is bright red with black leather interior and polished factory 16" rims.  The body is all fiberglass much like an older Corvette.  After spending quite a bit of time around, in, and working on his car, I am not so impressed anymore.  <P>He has the four cylinder turbo model.  It is a rather noisy engine kind of like the stock 2.5 Fiero.  You have to really turn it up to get into the boost.  The pedals are very close together and in a narrow tunnel below the dash.  The seats are not very comfortable and the bottons and knobs are hard to recognized and reach.<P>He has had problems with almost everything on the car.  Believe it or not, the headlight motors are exactly the same as the 87-88 Fiero and I have replaced them both.  <P>I must say, it is fun to be seen in it, and have it sitting in the garage.  People would drive past my house slow looking in the garage wondering what I do for a living.  That was fun.<P>You can get a good 1990 for around $18 to $30 depending on how desperate the current owner is. The 1990 to 00 models look almost identical.  The difference being the V8.   My friend would probably sell his for around $20.  <P>||||reg||1
